WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.006
- Please welcome, Hailey Bennett.

00:00:02.006 --> 00:00:05.256
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.034 --> 00:00:09.567
It's so wonderful to see you.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.597
- This is for you.
- Oh!

00:00:11.597 --> 00:00:12.680
Oh my God,

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.365
I'm so happy to see you.
- Hi.

00:00:15.365 --> 00:00:16.813
I'm so happy to see you.
(audience applauding)

00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:20.780
I promised myself I
wouldn't cry and here I am.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.550
- Should I open it now or wait?

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.420
- Open it now.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.120
- Okay.
(exclaims excitedly)

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.156
- Oh, Hailey, I'm so happy for your life.

00:00:28.156 --> 00:00:29.330
- Thank you.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.523
- We weren't moms when we did

00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:32.630
- I know.
- "Music and Lyrics"

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.370
a billion years ago.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.680
We were just kids.
- I know.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.610
Yes.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.640
It was my first time in New
York, when we made the film.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.180
And I was just so in awe, I was so...

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.560
I'm from Ohio, I was just so in awe

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.650
of being in the big city,
doing a film with you,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.710
with Hugh, Drew and Hugh,

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.690
and I remember the casting
director, lovely Eileen,

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.070
she said, "Can you learn a dance?"

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.140
Can I learn a dance?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.120
I'm not a dancer.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:07.010
So I went to like, one of
Britney Spear's former dancers

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.480
to teach me a dance in the valley.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.250
And the next day I was meant
to fly for this screen test

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.910
and I remember like
being down on all fours

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.157
and just stopping and being like,

00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:21.092
"I'm so sorry I can't do this."

00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:22.035
(audience laughing)

00:01:22.035 --> 00:01:23.585
I was so embarrassed

00:01:23.585 --> 00:01:25.890
and they were so wonderful and gracious.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.420
I'm like, "I'm so sorry, I should,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.920
I think I'm gonna go back to Ohio now."

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.800
Like get the first plane back to Ohio.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.750
- [Drew] And yet-
- [Hailey] And yet.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.540
- That was the beginning of a
long and illustrious career.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.948
I mean, you have not stopped working

00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:42.245
(audience applauding)
since then, ever.

00:01:42.245 --> 00:01:44.150
- [Hailey] Thank you.
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.680
You're not going to believe this.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.310
All I've wanted is fingerless gloves,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.339
thank you for answering my prayer.

00:01:48.339 --> 00:01:49.532
(audience applauding)
- They were hand knit.

00:01:49.532 --> 00:01:51.062
- [Drew] Hand knit?
- [Hailey] Hand knit.

00:01:51.062 --> 00:01:52.259
(audience applauding)
- Oh, they're so beautiful.

00:01:52.259 --> 00:01:53.900
- For you, with love.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.850
- And this is such an intimate gift.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.120
Like, I'll be thinking of
you and holding your heart

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.010
and my heart in your hand knit gloves.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.020
Thank you so much.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.210
Fingerless, thank you.
- Fingerless.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.800
- Okay, so you did get
the part and then...

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.541
Holy cow, I'm sorry, your
shoes are so incredible.

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:15.200
In fact,
(audience applauding)

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.090
might they not be a
beautiful dovetail and parlay

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:22.240
into how did you celebrate
that win of winning the part?

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.970
- Well, so I was living
very close to Fifth Avenue

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.970
and I marched my way over to
Fifth Avenue and bought shoes.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.850
And ever since then I've had a
great love affair with shoes.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:38.110
But they were the most amazing,
green Marc Jacob's shoes

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.570
and they were so expensive.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.403
- Yeah.

00:02:41.403 --> 00:02:44.020
- And now I have a whole closet full

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.820
of overly expensive shoes.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.080
- Carrie Bradshaw?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.450
- Like, major Carrie
Bradshaw, maybe worse.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.570
But also, the other thing that I bought

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.270
was a bottle of perfume, which
there's a little bit left

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.550
and I'm saving it for my wedding.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.810
- And you're engaged.
- Yes.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:05.810
- And your fiance, Joe Wright
is one of the most renowned,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.060
important filmmakers in our industry.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.720
If you love "Pride and
Prejudice", "Atonement", "Hanna",

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.690
you name it, it is all, "Anna Karenina",

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.546
all from the mind of your
extraordinary fiance.

00:03:18.546 --> 00:03:21.796
(audience applauding)

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.070
Now you're doing "Cyrano" with him.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.210
What is it like to be in love

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.880
with the man who is directing you?

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.140
What is that like?

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.833
- A lot of pressure.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.730
Although yeah, it works for some people,

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.780
it doesn't work for other people.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.200
It really works for us.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.750
We're looking forward to
making more films together

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.700
and it's great, yeah.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.440
And he's the most incredible,
like humble, loving,

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.330
kind, you know, the heart
that goes into his films

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.218
it's just, it's unlike anyone

00:03:59.218 --> 00:04:00.930
I've ever worked with.
- Can you trust him more?

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.370
- Like, cause-
- Yeah.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:05.200
- If a really renowned director
is telling me what to do

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.030
I'm like, "Great, I wanna
know what you think.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.440
I have my own arsenal to
work with, I want yours."

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.590
- Absolutely.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.440
There is so much trust involved
between actor and director,

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.930
so to already show up with
that established was, yeah,

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.583
was really, was really useful.

00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:25.166
(upbeat music)

